# CGI prefix UNDER the docroot, so the only path at which the shipped page can
# reach the shipped CGI is $DOCROOT/cgi-bin/p5-portal. The portal's README names
# both ways to get it there -- "symlinked or installed at <docroot>/cgi-bin/
# p5-portal" (deploy/p5/portal/README.md, the Install section) -- and only one of
# them is expressible here: p5-install places FILES and records them by sha256,
# so a symlink would be a path nothing recorded and --remove would leave behind.
# The CGI resolves its own library from $P5_PORTAL_DIR
# (deploy/p5/portal/cgi/p5-portal:30), never from its own directory, so moving
# the destination one level changes nothing it does. Its repo path is unchanged;
# only the dest differs from the README's table row, which is the symlink
# variant's source location.
#
# THE FIVE DIRECTORY ROWS ARE NOT DECORATION. A directory p5-install creates
# only as `place`'s `mkdir -p` parent is NEVER recorded and NEVER rmdir-ed
# (p5/bin/p5-install:495-501 says so in its own comment), so without a `dir` row
# per level the portal's tree would survive --remove empty, and the P5-half
# clean predicate would correctly call the box NOT CLEAN -- wedged against its
# own reinstall. state=install for the dirs (the installer makes them on every
# client install) and state=reserved for the eight files (they come FROM THE
# PACKAGE via the filemap, exactly like the validators, so they must stay out of
# the state=install set IN-14/IN-15 cross-check against the installer's own
# synthesised list).
